inspiration/

# Local working directories — kept out of clone weight.
# Source PNGs live in design-assets/; the exported, in-app versions are
# committed under frontend/public/assets/ and ARE tracked, because the app
# cannot render the tree without them.
.tmp/
design-assets/
screenshots/
# Mobile-view mockups and the skill that reads them. The *.md rule below
# already covers the skill file, but not the PNGs sitting beside it — and
# these are design material, so the whole directory goes.
phoneview/
# Full-resolution sources for the README media. The compressed, committed
# versions live under .github/media/ — the raw recording alone is ~36 MB.
github-assets/

# Documentation and agent scaffolding stay local.
# The repo carries code only. Build docs (docs/, NEXT_STEPS.md, CLAUDE.md)
# and the frontend-identity skill live on the working machine, not in git.
# Deliberately a blanket rule so a new doc is never committed by accident —
# no code reads a .md file, so nothing breaks. If a README is ever wanted,
# add `!README.md` here rather than dropping this line.
*.md

# The one exception, taken deliberately: the repo's public front page. Everything
# else (docs/, NEXT_STEPS.md, CLAUDE.md) stays local, so README.md must be
# self-contained — it cannot link to a sibling doc a cloner will never receive.
# Anchored with a leading slash: a bare `!README.md` matches at every depth and
# would also drag in frontend/README.md, which is still Vite's boilerplate.
!/README.md

# Agent scaffolding: skills, their reference images, local permissions.
# The whole directory, not just *.md — skills bundle PNG references, and those
# are exactly the design images that must stay out of the repo.
.claude/
